# blender-execution

## Overview
Functional capability to execute Blender via command line, run Python scripts, create assets, and manage export pipelines.

## When to Use
- Need to create 3D models programmatically
- Want to batch process 3D assets
- Need to render images/videos from Blender
- Creating game assets for export
- Automating 3D workflows
- Running Blender Python scripts

## Blender Installation Path
```javascript
const BLENDER_PATHS = {
    windows: 'C:/Program Files/Blender Foundation/Blender 5.1/blender.exe',
    mac: '/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender',
    linux: '/usr/bin/blender'
};
```

## Blender Command Line

### Launch Blender Headless
```javascript
// Via Node.js exec
const { exec } = require('child_process');

const blenderPath = 'C:/Program Files/Blender Foundation/Blender 5.1/blender.exe';

function runBlenderScript(scriptPath) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        exec(`"${blenderPath}" --background --python "${scriptPath}"`, 
            (error, stdout, stderr) => {
                if (error) reject(error);
                else resolve(stdout);
            }
        );
    });
}
```

### Common Flags
| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--background` | Run without GUI |
| `--python <file>` | Execute Python script |
| `--python-expr <code>` | Execute Python expression |
| `-o <path>` | Output path for renders |
| `-f` | Render single frame |
| `-a` | Render animation |
| `-E <engine>` | Render engine (CYCLES, EEVEE) |

### Examples
```javascript
// Render single frame
async function renderFrame(blendFile, outputPath, frame) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        exec(`"${blenderPath}" -b "${blendFile}" -o "${outputPath}" -f ${frame}`,
            (err, stdout, stderr) => err ? reject(err) : resolve(stdout));
    });
}

// Run Python script
async function runScript(scriptPath) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        exec(`"${blenderPath}" --background --python "${scriptPath}"`,
            (err, stdout, stderr) => err ? reject(err) : resolve(stdout));
    });
}

// Export GLTF
async function exportGLTF(blendFile, outputPath) {
    const script = `
import bpy
bpy.ops.export_scene.gltf(filepath="${outputPath.replace(/\\/g, '/')}")
`;
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        exec(`"${blenderPath}" --background --python-expr "${script}"`,
            (err, stdout, stderr) => err ? reject(err) : resolve(stdout));
    });
}
```

