# sprite-execution

## Overview
Functional capability to create 2D sprites, pixel art, sprite sheets, and animated game assets programmatically.

## When to Use
- Need to generate pixel art programmatically
- Creating game sprites for Unity/Godot/Three.js
- Building sprite sheets from individual frames
- Converting images to pixel art
- Creating tile-based game assets

## Canvas Setup

### Initialize Pixel Canvas
```javascript
function createPixelCanvas(width, height, pixelSize = 4) {
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = width * pixelSize;
    canvas.height = height * pixelSize;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
    return { canvas, ctx, pixelSize, width, height };
}

// Usage
const sprite = createPixelCanvas(16, 16, 4); // 16x16 pixels, 4x scale
```

### Draw Pixel
```javascript
function drawPixel(sprite, x, y, color) {
    sprite.ctx.fillStyle = color;
    sprite.ctx.fillRect(
        x * sprite.pixelSize, 
        y * sprite.pixelSize, 
        sprite.pixelSize, 
        sprite.pixelSize
    );
}

